From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:10:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(client): xhttp transport with sing-box-extended

Build-If: variant=homeproxy sb=extended

The xhttp transport of Xray is in sing-box-extended and podkop-engine,
not in the official sing-box. Support it where the core has it:

- homeproxy.uc and rpcd: singBoxHasXHTTP() / hp_has_xhttp ask the core
  with "sing-box check" of a one outbound config; the build tags do not
  tell. The answer is cached per binary (size and mtime), so a core
  replaced by apk is asked again.
- node.js: XHTTP in the transport list with host, path, mode, padding
  and "extra settings": the extra JSON of an Xray link (headers, xmux,
  downloadSettings and the rest). Without a core that has xhttp the
  entry says so and a node with it cannot be saved.
- Subscriptions and the share link import: xhttp and splithttp links
  are read (host, path, mode, extra as JSON or base64, x_padding_bytes
  of 3x-ui) when the core has xhttp, otherwise skipped as before.
- generate_client.uc: the node becomes an xhttp transport. Extra is
  mapped to the sing-box names (with the old session names and
  downloadSettings with TLS or REALITY), Host moves out of the headers
  (sing-box refuses it there), zero ranges mean the default and the
  padding is never empty ("x_padding_bytes cannot be disabled"). An
  unknown or invalid extra is reported in the log and left out.
- If the core has no xhttp (e.g. the official sing-box after apk
  upgrade) such a node becomes a block outbound with a log line: its
  traffic is dropped instead of the whole configuration being refused,
  and it is never sent direct.
- The log lines of the generator carry the time and [DAEMON], like the
  rest of the homeproxy log.

Without xhttp nodes the generated configuration is byte-identical to
before (7 test configurations, sing-box 1.14.2 and
1.14.1-extended-2.7.2).

Checked: share links of vless, trojan and vmess with xhttp, splithttp,
extra as JSON and base64, an invalid extra, through the real parse_uri
and parseShareLink, then the generator and "sing-box check" on both
cores (also custom routing with bind_interface, detour and
domain_resolver, and a URLTest group); a live loopback with
sing-box-extended as the xhttp server and the generated outbound as the
client: auto, packet-up, stream-up and stream-one, plain and over TLS,
3 MB files byte-identical, three parallel downloads, extra with headers,
xmux, padding and sc_max_each_post_bytes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
